    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d546">

                <pb facs="0627" n="534" sameAs="frus:frus1935v04/pg534"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">822.00 Revolutions/72: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Ecuador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Gonzalez</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-10-01T18:00:00-05:00">October 1, 1935—6
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>22. Your 45, September 28, noon, and 46, September 29, 4 p.m. Could it be
                    maintained that Paez, who is understood to have been Minister of Public Works in
                    the cabinet of ex-President Pons, succeeded <pb facs="0628" n="535"
                        xml:id="pg535"/> to the presidency in accordance with the provisions of
                    Article 79 of the Constitution of March 26, 1929?<anchor n="29" xml:id="d546-f1"
                    /> Cable your comments.</p>
                <p>Also, advise Department of any specific information relating to the “downright
                    social reforms” which, as reported in your 45, Paez has announced his intention
                    to initiate immediately.</p>
                <p>Have you as yet received any official communication from the Minister of Foreign
                    Affairs of the Paez Government announcing its assumption of power?</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d546-f1" n="29" xml:id="d546-f1-content">
